    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "A tank was 3/4 full and Ravi used 1/3 of the water.\n\"How much is left?\" asked Meena."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "of",
     "reciprocal",
     "check"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To solve fraction problems read carefully, decide whether to multiply or divide and write the operation. 'Of' means multiply.\n1/3 of 3/4 is 1/3 times 3/4, which is 1/4. So he used 1/4 of the tank and 3/4 minus 1/4 is 1/2 of the tank is left.\nCheck that the answer is sensible: the amount left must be smaller than what we started with."
    }
   },
